WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:06.100
I want a game out with you guys, the various
possible outcomes for the 2020 election, but

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.990
I admit I'm sort of scared to do this on the
show because there will be people in the audience

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.980
who will misunderstand what I'm doing either
deliberately or they will just misunderstand

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:15.980
it.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.400
There will be people in the audience who think
that I am in this segment going to suggest

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:25.109
we support someone other than a real progressive
in 2020 and I want to be clear, I'm doing

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:27.699
this segment because this is what we do on
the show.

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:31.919
This is the type of thing that over the years
people have come to appreciate about the show.

00:00:31.919 --> 00:00:36.780
We think about things, we consider possibilities,
we discuss them, but let me put this in front

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.910
of everything so that I am not misunderstood.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:44.760
We should vote for the person whose values
and policies most closely match ours and I

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.750
am a progressive, so I believe we should vote
for a progressive.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:53.240
Now, that being said, that disclaimer, given
I want to game out 2020 with you.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:59.880
Let's imagine for basic scenarios for 2020
think about it like a two by two grid.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.670
On one side, there's the possibility that
Democrats nominate either a centrist or a

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.670
progressive.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:10.390
For this example, we could say Biden or Bernie,
you could say Klobuchar or Warren.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:15.340
If you want to go by the New York times endorsements,
whatever the Democrats could nominate a centrist

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.000
or a progressive along the other axis is the
possibility that Donald Trump either wins

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.289
reelection or loses it.

00:01:22.289 --> 00:01:24.290
This gives us four possible outcomes.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:28.650
You could nominate a progressive and see them
lose to Trump, or you could nominate a progressive

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.999
and see them defeat Trump and become president.

00:01:30.999 --> 00:01:37.270
You could also see a centrist nominated and
lose to Donald Trump, or you can see a Centrus

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.499
nominated and defeat Donald Trump.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:45.729
I want to explore with you whether the best
outcome for the longterm for Progressive's

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:54.310
might be that a centrist like Joe Biden be
nominated but lose to Donald Trump in 2020

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.889
I've read some articles about this over the
last few months and I want to think through

00:01:57.889 --> 00:01:59.219
the scenarios with you.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:05.689
Let's first imagine that a is nominated but
loses to Trump in November.

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:11.750
This is bad for the progressive movement because
it will be used not only by the right, but

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:16.560
it'll even be used by the centrists left to
say, look, you got a shot.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.300
You nominated a progressive and they lost.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:25.240
This proves we can't move the party to the
left centrism and moderation and trying to

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:30.470
compromise with crazy Republicans is the path
forward and that could damage the left for

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.420
a long time to come.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:38.550
Next scenario would be that a progressive
is nominated and wins defeats Donald Trump

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:45.350
in 2020 in this case, that progressive would
have to govern with a likely Republican Senate

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:50.260
for at least two years, if not more, and the
serious possibility of losing control of the

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.560
house in the midterms.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.040
As often happens when you have a party change
in a presidential election, the next midterm,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.470
the party that takes control in the presidential
loses control of the house.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:04.710
Now none of that's guaranteed, but particularly
with the Republican Senate, and especially

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:09.560
if Democrats lose control of the house in
2022 this would be a progressive president

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:15.180
who will undoubtedly fail to accomplish many
of their major campaign promises and it would

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.290
also be called a major defeat for the progressive
left.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.510
Look, you got someone in there and they didn't
do a damn thing.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.410
Republicans will take advantage.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:29.150
Centrist Democrats will say, look, you won
and you couldn't do anything in 2022 and in

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.540
2024 and beyond.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.730
There are counter arguments and we'll get
to them later.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.760
We're being thorough here.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.980
Next possibility.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:42.610
A centrist like Joe Biden wins the nomination
and defeats Trump in 2020 now to a lot of

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:47.730
us, this feels very unlikely, myself included,
but let's imagine that Biden is nominated

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.040
and wins.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.740
This is of course terrible for the progressive
movement because Joe Biden's not a progressive.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:58.569
This would allow the centrist Democrats to
claim the way to fight the right is with a

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:00.290
moderate like Joe Biden.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:04.260
They'll say, look, we nominated a centrist
and a centrist one.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.670
They will say, that's evidence that progressivism
is not the way to go.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:12.130
Now, Biden of course won't do anything hugely
progressive because he's not a progressive

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:14.550
and the center left will say, this is the
way to go.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:17.260
This is how you win with a centrist Democrat.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:21.190
That could also damage the progressive movement
for a long time.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:27.740
So then we get to scenario number four, which
again, is this the best game theory outcome,

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:33.850
which is that a Biden or another centrist
is nominated, but they lose to Donald Trump

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:39.970
in November of 2020 in the long term, this
might be the best for the progressive movement.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:44.910
Number one, it would continue to provide support
for the idea that the way to beat the right

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:49.260
is not with a centrist because you'll have
Hillary having lost to Trump and Biden having

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.790
lost to Trump.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.170
That's a real strong case that it's really
time for a progressive.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.620
A centrist would have been nominated and lost
again.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:01.840
We would also get another four years of an
even more unhinged and erratic Trump who no

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:06.220
longer has to run for reelection, who would
likely be even crazier than the Trump of the

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:13.180
first term, and this might further justify
supporting a true progressive as the obvious

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:19.350
and only way to go in 2024 now, of course,
that would be a pretty bad four years for

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.880
the United States of America.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.530
So I'm not here to suggest we elect Joe Biden.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.770
I'm not voting for Joe Biden in the primary.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:30.800
I'm not here to suggest we allow Donald Trump
to win in 2020 what I'm presenting to you

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:36.020
from a game theory perspective is the possibility
that over the long term, the progressive left

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:42.370
might benefit from Biden being the nominee
and losing to Trump despite it being an absolutely

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.740
horrible outcome for the country in the immediate.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.560
Now there are many counter arguments to be
made.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.880
Let's make some of them.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:54.490
One is a progressive president elected in
2020 wouldn't lose the house in 2022 uh, nor

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:58.290
would they suffer from a Republican Senate
the entire presidency.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:02.790
They might not get it in 2020 but they could
likely get it in 2022 and then they could

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.760
actually get some things done.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.650
They could put in place some of the most significant
progressive change in history.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:10.650
That's a possibility.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.970
That would be a counter argument that one
could make.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:18.540
It would require a reversal from historic
trends, but it is a completely valid counter

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:19.950
argument to what I'm suggesting.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:25.300
Another counter argument would be there are
people who feel super strongly that Bernie

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:31.530
and Warren simply would not lose to Trump,
and that they would get a lot done.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.970
Let me know what you think.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.830
Game it out with me.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.890
And again, we're, we're talking like adults
here.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.560
I'm voting for a progressive and I'm voting
to defeat Donald Trump.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:08:40.750
This is a conversation that I'm having with
you about the four possible outcomes.

